##" Every US public library system and branch in the IMLS Public Libraries Survey: FY2023 in detail, plus every system FY2018 - FY2024 (use, spend, e-content and print budgets) and US Census county population 2010 - 2025, so library use and spend can be read per county resident and against population growth. Built to answer buyer questions: which libraries an e-book vendor should call (econtent_prospects -> libraries_to_pitch_digital_content), how big the library e-content market is (library_years -> econtent_market_by_year), which fast-growing counties underfund their libraries and what closing the gap costs (county_spend_gap -> fast_growing_counties_underfunding_libraries), value per dollar by system size (library_years -> systems_by_size_value_per_dollar) and recovery since 2019 (library_years -> library_use_recovery_since_2019). Defaults to North Carolina; pick any state.
## dataset { title="US Public Libraries (FY2018 - FY2024)" }

import { library_systems, library_branches, library_years, county_population, county_libraries, econtent_candidates, econtent_prospects, county_spend_gap, STATE, SIZE_BAND } from 'libraries.malloy'

export { library_systems, library_branches, library_years, county_population, county_libraries, econtent_candidates, econtent_prospects, county_spend_gap, STATE, SIZE_BAND }
